Package: miadi-tide
Version: 0.1.0
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), tmux, jq, python3-venv (>= 3.11) | python3.12-venv | python3.11-venv
Maintainer: Miadi <mia@jgwill.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/jgwill/miadi-orchestration-kit
Description: The tide review loop and runtime on a Miadi host
 Review an agent's last reply in a tmux pane, annotate it, and hand the
 review back to the agent:
  tan <target>              review and deliver on submit
  plannotator-tmux-review   the loop itself (options: --help)
  plannotator-tui           the annotator, built from the Miadi fork
 The tide runtime (ironsilk, the `tide` CLI) runs in its own venv,
 /usr/lib/miadi-tide/tide-runtime, built at install only from the pinned
 wheels in the package. It needs Python 3.11 or newer: python3-venv on
 Ubuntu 24.04, python3.12-venv from the deadsnakes PPA on 22.04. The
 @miadi/tide and @miadi/tide-contract sources are in
 /usr/share/miadi-tide/node/.
 .
 Client: tide, tan, plannotator-tmux-review, plannotator-tui, @miadi/tide.
 Server: `tide daemon`, as the user units tide-runtime.service and
 tide-store-prune.timer, off until a user enables them.
